# Generated artefacts
reports/*.pdf
reports/*.png
reports/**/*.nc
reports/*.log
data/cache/

# Phase 4 live-predict bundle exception: the trained per-lead Bayesian
# posteriors are needed by legacy predict paths at inference time.
# ~10 MB per lead (3 leads = ~30 MB total) — fine to track directly
# until the bundle grows enough to warrant LFS or an R2-side artefact store.
!reports/phase4_artefacts/bayesian_predictions/posteriors/*.nc

# Phase 5a bundle: NOT tracked in git. retrain-python.yml pushes to
# r2:${R2_BUCKET}/reports/phase5a_artefacts/ at every fit, predict-5a.yml
# pulls the same paths at every cron tick. Matches the 4a pattern
# (predict-4a.yml rclone-pulls data/models/precipitation/**/*phase4a*/**).
# The previous "track posterior .nc in git" exception above (now removed)
# meant predict-5a effectively pinned to whatever was last committed,
# auto-retrain on R2 couldn't take effect, and bundle binaries bloated
# the repo. Note: training_summary.json + the research CSVs at the
# phase5a_artefacts/ root level remain tracked (small text, useful diffs).
reports/phase5a_artefacts/live_bundle/
reports/phase5a_artefacts/posteriors/
reports/phase5a_artefacts/predictions/
reports/phase5a_artefacts_spread/live_bundle/
reports/phase5a_artefacts_spread/posteriors/
